{"name":"Sepia","hex":"#704214","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Sepia","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Sepiidae – many cuttlefishes, including many of the most common ones."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Sepia"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sepia (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Sepia is a reddish-brown color, named after the rich brown pigment derived from the ink sac of the common cuttlefish Sepia. The word sepia is the Latinized form of the Ancient Greek word σηπία, meaning cuttlefish."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Codex_Atlanticus_-_000V-26.jpg/330px-Codex_Atlanticus_-_000V-26.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sepia_(color)"},{"title":"Photographic print toning","blocks":[{"text":"In photography, toning is a method of altering the color of monochrome photography. In analog photography, it is a chemical process carried out on metal salt-based prints, such as silver prints, iron-based prints, or platinum or palladium prints. This darkroom process cannot be performed with a color photograph. The effects of this process can be emulated with software in digital photography. Sepia toning, the most familiar such process, is considered a form of black-and-white or monochrome photography."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Departure_of_Bushmens_contingent_%286128313991%29.jpg/330px-Departure_of_Bushmens_contingent_%286128313991%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Photographic_print_toning"},{"title":"Sepia (cephalopod)","blocks":[{"text":"Sepia is a genus of cuttlefish in the family Sepiidae encompassing some of the best known and most common species. The cuttlebone is ellipsoid in shape. The name of the genus is the Latinised form of the Ancient Greek σηπία (sēpía) \"cuttlefish\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/HPIM1795.JPG/330px-HPIM1795.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sepia_(cephalopod)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Ice_Cream_Dreams%2C_by_Chris_Marchant.jpg/500px-Ice_Cream_Dreams%2C_by_Chris_Marchant.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Ice_Cream_Dreams%2C_by_Chris_Marchant.jpg/1280px-Ice_Cream_Dreams%2C_by_Chris_Marchant.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Ice_Cream_Dreams%2C_by_Chris_Marchant.jpg/500px-Ice_Cream_Dreams%2C_by_Chris_Marchant.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIce_Cream_Dreams%2C_by_Chris_Marchant.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Roma_a6_-_Augusto_De_Luca_fotografo.jpg/500px-Roma_a6_-_Augusto_De_Luca_fotografo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Roma_a6_-_Augusto_De_Luca_fotografo.jpg/500px-Roma_a6_-_Augusto_De_Luca_fotografo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A sepia-toned photograph, Palazzo della Civiltà Italiana Rome, Augusto De Luca, 1995","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoma_a6_-_Augusto_De_Luca_fotografo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/MalibuColor.jpg/120px-MalibuColor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/MalibuColor.jpg/250px-MalibuColor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content